    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">Captain Paul is the owner and lead expedition guide of Supernova Expeditions. He brings a lifetime of experience as a mariner, scuba diver, commercial pilot, entrepreneur and global adventurer to every trip.</p>
      <p>A licensed U.S. Coast Guard Master Captain, Paul holds a 100 ton credential with towing and radio operator endorsements. He has safely logged thousands of nautical miles throughout the Pacific Northwest, Canada and beyond.</p>
      <h2>Nova, first mate and cook</h2>
      <p>Paul is often joined by his wife Nova, who inspired the name Supernova Expeditions. Nova is a highly capable first mate and cook, and she brings a relentless, contagious positive attitude to every kind of trip.</p>
      <h2>Before Supernova</h2>
      <p>Paul spent decades building and leading companies: 12 startup ventures, including taking a company public and serving as a public company CEO.</p>
      <p>He's also a commercial, instrument rated pilot with over 3,000 flight hours and two world aviation records. He brings the same precision and leadership to life at sea.</p>
      <h2>Why Supernova</h2>
      <p>Paul chose Supernova, his custom 78 foot adventure motor yacht, to reflect a spirit of purpose and possibility. Whether he's leading scuba diving expeditions, remote wilderness trips or training new mariners, he blends technical skill with a deep love of nature and storytelling.</p>
      <p>His goal is to help guests reconnect with the natural world, push their limits a little and come home with stories worth telling.</p>
      <p><strong>With Captain Paul at the helm, every Supernova voyage is not just a trip. It's an expedition.</strong></p>
